<title>JAPAN: Ontario launches 3.1% yen/A$ rvse dual samurai.</title>
<headline>Ontario launches 3.1% yen/A$ rvse dual samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar reverse dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Nomura Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Province of Ontario</p>
<p> AMT		 5.0 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.1 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  16 March 2007</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  18 March 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Feb 27 to Feb 28</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA-, Moody's Aa3</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTES: The coupon will be paid in dollars, while redemption will be in yen. The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,247.14 to 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
